1
00:00:08,060 --> 00:01:07,860
You're Tops

2
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:10,540
Is that you, Susan?

3
00:01:10,540 --> 00:01:12,730
It's me, Grandpa.

4
00:01:12,730 --> 00:01:14,500
Am I glad to see you!

5
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:17,800
And am I glad to see you!

6
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:21,350
I am also glad to be here.

7
00:01:21,350 --> 00:01:23,350
How are things?

8
00:01:23,350 --> 00:01:26,260
I have been talking to a group of salesmen

9
00:01:26,260 --> 00:01:27,820
since ten this morning,

10
00:01:27,820 --> 00:01:31,020
and I'm real exhausted.

11
00:01:31,020 --> 00:01:33,540
Well, you look good.

12
00:01:33,540 --> 00:01:34,730
What's Harry doing tonight?

13
00:01:34,730 --> 00:01:35,200
He and Michelle

14
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:38,190
are visiting relatives in New Jersey today.

15
00:01:38,190 --> 00:01:40,710
The rest of our family went to the movies.

16
00:01:40,710 --> 00:01:43,990
So it's just you and me, Susan.

17
00:01:43,990 --> 00:01:46,880
It's nice to be alone with you, Grandpa.

18
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:48,720
We don't get to see enough of each other.

19
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:50,870
Oh, I feel the same way, Susan.

20
00:01:50,870 --> 00:01:53,600
I miss seeing you.

21
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:55,400
But to tell the truth,

22
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:56,650
next time

23
00:01:56,650 --> 00:01:58,660
I'd like to go into the city and meet you there,

24
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:01,970
instead of you coming here.

25
00:02:01,970 --> 00:02:03,650
You don't need to do that, Grandpa.

26
00:02:03,650 --> 00:02:05,690
Yeah, I do.

27
00:02:05,690 --> 00:02:09,750
I need to get out more.

28
00:02:09,750 --> 00:02:11,930
Well, I mean

29
00:02:11,930 --> 00:02:14,000
there's a lot to do around the house,

30
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:15,700
and I love being here with the family,

31
00:02:15,700 --> 00:02:16,430
you know,

32
00:02:16,430 --> 00:02:20,850
but I'm restless.

33
00:02:20,850 --> 00:02:22,860
Since I retired,

34
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:25,820
I've got extra time on my hands.

35
00:02:25,820 --> 00:02:29,110
I understand, Grandpa.

36
00:02:29,110 --> 00:02:31,260
I think you do.

37
00:02:31,260 --> 00:02:32,950
Frankly,

38
00:02:32,950 --> 00:02:36,280
I'd like to use my brain a little more.

39
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:37,540
Grandpa,

40
00:02:37,540 --> 00:02:42,100
you have so much energy and so many years of experience.

41
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:45,230
There are probably a lot of places for you to work

42
00:02:45,230 --> 00:02:48,250
Particularly in the construction field.

43
00:02:48,250 --> 00:02:50,290
But at my age,

44
00:02:50,290 --> 00:02:52,920
I'm not looking for a full-time job.

45
00:02:52,920 --> 00:02:56,050
I'm retired.

46
00:02:56,050 --> 00:02:57,390
But I'm bored.

47
00:02:57,390 --> 00:03:03,030
Well, there must be something.

48
00:03:03,030 --> 00:03:07,340
Maybe I can help.

49
00:03:07,340 --> 00:03:09,310
Let's go into the kitchen,

50
00:03:09,310 --> 00:03:12,740
and maybe you can help me set the table.

51
00:03:12,740 --> 00:03:14,180
Sounds good to me.

52
00:03:14,180 --> 00:03:15,310
What are we having?

53
00:03:15,310 --> 00:03:17,510
I prepared lamb chops,

54
00:03:17,510 --> 00:03:20,770
mashed potatoes, and a tossed green salad to begin with.

55
00:03:20,770 --> 00:03:34,110
Grandpa, you are a terrific guy!

56
00:03:34,110 --> 00:03:36,780
You're still thinking about something to do, aren't you?

57
00:03:36,780 --> 00:03:38,180
A job of some kind.

58
00:03:38,180 --> 00:03:40,130
That's right.

59
00:03:40,130 --> 00:03:44,340
I've been thinking about it for weeks now.

60
00:03:44,340 --> 00:03:49,330
There must be some way to put my mind to good use.

61
00:03:49,330 --> 00:03:50,860
We'll find a solution.

62
00:03:50,860 --> 00:03:52,360
A positive solution

63
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:55,360
to your finding a way to use that wonderful mind of yours.
